Tools (runtime dependencies)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

faster-whisper — MIT License, © SYSTRAN. Built on CTranslate2.
  Provides the `WhisperModel` runtime used by the optional in-training CER eval
  (`diamond/training/eval_cer.py`). Optional `eval` extra.
  Source: https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper

Silero VAD — MIT License, © Silero Team.
  Used offline to extract the committed `augmentation/noise_bank/` silence and
  background segments. Not a runtime training dependency.
  Source: https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad

FFmpeg — invoked as an external binary (subprocess) by the DSP augmentor
  (`augmentation/augment_pipeline.py`) for MP3/AAC/OGG codec simulation. Not
  bundled or linked; governed by the license of the FFmpeg build you install
  (typically LGPL-2.1+ or GPL depending on the build).
  Source: https://ffmpeg.org

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Datasets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Training uses the public speech corpora listed in `configs/pilot.yaml`
(`data.studio_sources`): LibriTTS-R, HiFi-TTS, VCTK, EARS, and Expresso. Each
carries its own license and citation requirements — see the corresponding
Hugging Face dataset cards.

The augmentation target pool (`nineninesix/emolia_filtered_features`) holds
degradation fingerprints — numeric channel features, no audio.

The committed noise samples in `augmentation/noise_bank/` are non-speech noise
segments drawn from the Emolia corpus (background/silence only, no speech),
extracted with Silero VAD. They ship in this repository, so their terms travel
with any redistribution — see the Emolia dataset terms.

The optional broadband-noise / RIR track (`data.noise_aug`) expects MUSAN or DNS
noise and OpenSLR-28 room impulse responses, which you supply yourself; this
repository neither ships nor downloads them.
